{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:09:47.969552Z","id":"752df0eb3fd7e4dff7330d7360191353d222cbfa90e1b4f81db389badfec04bc","body":{"detail":"`SyncRecord` has no `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]` (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:28-52), and neither did the 0.29.0 struct. A 0.29.0 binary therefore loads a 0.30.0 manifest without complaint, drops `remotes` on read, and writes the manifest back without it. Every manifest write goes through `update_manifest`, which loads, changes and saves the whole file (engine.rs:540-545). In 0.29.0, `record_artifact` and `flush_writes` also replaced records wholesale (`.insert`/`.extend`), so one `p cache sync`, one `path query` auto-sync or one `p import` from an older install (for example a second machine on a shared home, or a downgrade) wipes the remote records of every session in the manifest. Separately, `load_manifest` still tells the user `parse {}; delete it to re-sync from scratch` (engine.rs:556). That was harmless while the manifest was a rebuildable index, but a resync cannot rebuild remote records: the server ids come only from the upload response. The CHANGELOG 0.30.0 entry says only `Manifests without the field load unchanged` (CHANGELOG.md:19-20) and does not mention that the format no longer survives an older binary. Nothing reads the records yet, so nothing fails today. Once incremental append reads them, a lost record makes the next share open a new graph instead of appending.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":47},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"9262ae34e2d345804720ebd0b5424729d329bd2bb9e2206707d1cc06c67f5049"},"suggested_fix":"Keep remote records in their own file (for example `$CONFIG_DIR/remotes.json`, keyed by artifact type and session id, written under the same lock), which older binaries never touch and the `delete it to re-sync` advice does not cover. If they stay in manifest.json, add a CHANGELOG line saying an older path-cli drops them, and change the parse-error message so it no longer tells users to delete the file.","summary":"Remote records live inside manifest.json, so running an older path-cli, or deleting the manifest as its parse error suggests, erases every record without a trace","tags":["review","review:pr-356-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:10:09.819718Z","id":"2b903d1db5fd68640490df3df7701cb4c1e61c5a294feb266230d97d6c2abb1d","body":{"detail":"`RemoteRecord::of` (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:79-87) accepts any stamp and `stamp_string` (engine.rs:94-103) renders `(None, None)` as \"/\". The engine's own freshness checks refuse an all-None stamp as unknowable: `record_is_current` (engine.rs:441-444) and `fresh_cache_id` (engine.rs:470-474) both require `modified.is_some() || size.is_some()`. Records with an all-None stamp are written in normal use: `p export pathbase <cache id>` of an entry from a remote import takes the stamp from the manifest record (`session_of_cache_id`, engine.rs ~483-494), and `reroot` clears that record's `modified` and `size` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_import/remote.rs:245-250); an opencode share always has `size: None` and has `modified: None` when the session is not listed (crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:244-249); a codex share whose rollout file is not found stats nothing (derive.rs:162-163). The doc comment on `stamp_string` says it is \"the same stamp the stat gate compares, so a pass can skip a session whose source has not moved\". A gate built on that, comparing \"/\" to \"/\", would decide that such a session has not moved and skip it forever. The cursor itself cannot tell \"no stamp\" from \"a stamp\", so this has to be fixed in the record shape before anything reads it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":79},"end":{"line":87},"content_hash":"d6f4b60331e11ff67d2913600001910e1cbbec205a8344f57f796ae8e07aebb9"},"suggested_fix":"Have `RemoteRecord::of` return `None` (record nothing) when both parts of the stamp are `None`, as the cache freshness checks already do. Or make `source_stamp` an `Option<String>` that is omitted when unknown, so a reader has to treat an unknown stamp as always stale. Add a test in engine.rs covering `RemoteRecord::of(path, (None, None))`.","summary":"RemoteRecord::of records an unknown source stamp (None, None) as the string \"/\", which a string-comparing stat gate will treat as a real stamp that never moves","tags":["review","review:pr-356-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:11:05.484585Z","id":"125f455d83db973bdcc6d850aecebc301196e8f41a7d581404c944acc87f8f77","body":{"detail":"`remotes` is stored inline on `SyncRecord` (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:47-51). Older path-cli versions use the same `~/.toolpath/manifest.json` and write it through `update_manifest` (engine.rs:540-545): load the whole manifest into their own `SyncRecord`, mutate it, then `save_manifest` it in full. serde ignores unknown fields by default (https://serde.rs/container-attrs.html#deny_unknown_fields), so an older binary drops `remotes` from every record it loads, not only the records it changes. Its next save erases them all. Any write by an older binary does this: a `p cache sync`, a `path query` auto-sync, a `p import`, a `p cache rm` eviction (`evict_cache_id`, engine.rs:498), or the pre-upload `record_artifact` in `path share`. The manifest has no version marker, so neither side can notice. Two binaries on one machine is a plausible setup: `path` from `cargo install path-cli` next to `path` from the deprecated `toolpath-cli` alias (crates/toolpath-cli/Cargo.toml), a pinned copy in a hook or plugin, or a downgrade. The test `manifest_without_remotes_loads` only covers the opposite direction, a new binary reading an old file. Once incremental append reads these records, losing one means the next share opens a new graph instead of appending.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":47},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"9262ae34e2d345804720ebd0b5424729d329bd2bb9e2206707d1cc06c67f5049"},"suggested_fix":"Keep remote records in their own file next to the manifest (e.g. `~/.toolpath/remotes.json`: artifact type -> session id -> url -> RemoteRecord), written under the same manifest lock. Older binaries never open that file, and `put_record` becomes unnecessary because sync and import no longer rewrite the struct that holds remotes. If the remotes stay inline, at least note in the CHANGELOG that running an older path-cli after 0.30.0 discards them.","summary":"Any manifest write by a path-cli older than 0.30.0 silently erases every session's `remotes`, because the older SyncRecord drops the unknown field on load and saves the manifest back without it","tags":["review","review:pr-356-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:11:05.484641Z","id":"d041fa029e0b2e645ce28a14e08a70ac6658f9d5c9e64adaeb4bfbdde30fce82","body":{"detail":"`run_pathbase_inner` always creates a new graph (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:1047-1068), so the key `remote_path_url` builds contains a new graph uuid on every upload. `record_remote` only replaces an entry with the same URL (engine.rs:108-132), so in practice it never replaces anything: sharing one session five times leaves five entries. `RemoteRecord` (engine.rs:63-73) holds `steps`, `last_step`, `head` and `source_stamp`, but no time it was written and no graph creation time. The map is a `BTreeMap<String, _>` ordered by URL, and graph uuids are random, so the order means nothing. A later reader (incremental append, `share --all`) that needs 'the path this session was last pushed to' cannot tell the latest share from an older one. Taking the largest `steps` breaks ties arbitrarily and still picks a graph the user has since deleted on the server. `source_stamp` cannot order them either, because records can share a stamp or have an empty one (`\"/\"`). The record shape is being fixed now, and adding the field later leaves every record written in between without it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"b39a7671fa4dab41c2b489c722492ecbfe954f1cb6e8990d1671f0e80f9737c6"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `pushed_at: DateTime<Utc>` (or reuse the `synced_at` convention from `SyncRecord`) to `RemoteRecord` and set it in `RemoteRecord::of`. Either document that the newest entry per server is the one to append to, or decide now that a new share of a session already recorded on the same server replaces the older entries for that server.","summary":"Each `path share` of a session adds a new key under a new graph uuid, and RemoteRecord carries no time or ordering, so a session's remotes map grows with every share and nothing says which entry is the current one","tags":["review","review:pr-356-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:11:05.484687Z","id":"9739e6ca149231bef8e1191c55a20b8a7af594b34ce790f71129088e1a999414","body":{"detail":"`SyncRecord` keeps the fingerprint as `modified: Option<DateTime<Utc>>` and `size: Option<u64>` (engine.rs:41-46). The stat gate compares those typed values and treats all-`None` as unknowable (`is_unchanged`, engine.rs:221-232; `record_is_current`). `RemoteRecord.source_stamp` (engine.rs:69-72) instead holds `stamp_string(stamp)`, `<rfc3339 AutoSi>/<size>`. To skip a session whose source has not moved since the push, a reader must call `stamp_string` again on a fresh stat and compare strings. That only works while the RFC 3339 formatting options never change, and the reader also has to know that `\"/\"` (`stamp_string((None, None))`) must never count as a match, which is the rule `is_unchanged` encodes for the typed fields. Both representations of one concept end up in the same file.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":94},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"4ec903042fc2f6a1c362816b78862a0c942262fe9a17ba82a205075823c81e39"},"suggested_fix":"Give `RemoteRecord` the same `modified`/`size` optional fields as `SyncRecord`, with the same serde attributes, and let a future gate share `is_unchanged`'s comparison. Drop `stamp_string`.","summary":"`source_stamp` stores the stat-gate stamp as a formatted string, while the manifest record next to it stores the same stamp as typed `modified`/`size`, so the future reader must re-render a stamp to compare it and handle `\"/\"` as 'unknowable' by hand","tags":["review","review:pr-356-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:11:31.804518Z","id":"a6dae2855625f55661b5c7f52fb06168b6ebd80d19070e72e3eaf5cd687cb7b2","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:79-87 `RemoteRecord::of` takes any stamp; :94-103 `stamp_string` formats (None, None) as \"/\" (unit test `stamp_string_leaves_absent_parts_empty` at :734). The cache checks refuse all-None stamps: engine.rs:441-443 (`record_is_current`) and :472-473 (`fresh_cache_id`) both require `rec.modified.is_some() || rec.size.is_some()`. All-None stamps do reach record_remotes: `session_of_cache_id` (engine.rs ~483-494) returns `(rec.modified, rec.size)` from the manifest; crates/path-cli/src/cmd_import/remote.rs:245-250 `reroot` sets provenance modified/size to None; crates/path-cli/src/derive.rs:162 codex gives (None, None) when the rollout file is missing; derive.rs:244-249 opencode modified is None when the session is not listed. The RemoteRecord doc (engine.rs:55-62) says \"Nothing reads these yet\", so there is no failure before merge, which fits concern.","kind":"comment","references":"2b903d1db5fd68640490df3df7701cb4c1e61c5a294feb266230d97d6c2abb1d","summary":"confirmed: an all-None stamp is recorded as \"/\" and is written in normal use; concern is the right kind since nothing reads the record yet","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:12:13.318737Z","id":"7ba00205f5fd069d010eeba732bcd1fa52f059c45e1de54b10d8fc7155459566","body":{"detail":"`git show origin/ben/jsonl-streaming-upload:crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs`: SyncRecord (line 28-29) derives Deserialize with no `remotes` field and no `deny_unknown_fields`, and update_manifest (line 426) loads the whole Manifest, mutates, and saves it in full. serde ignores unknown fields by default (https://serde.rs/container-attrs.html#deny_unknown_fields), so the reserialized manifest lacks `remotes` on every record. Current engine.rs:47-51 stores remotes inline on SyncRecord; no version marker exists in the manifest. Nothing consumes remotes yet, so concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"125f455d83db973bdcc6d850aecebc301196e8f41a7d581404c944acc87f8f77","summary":"confirmed: an older path-cli's full read-modify-write of the manifest drops every record's remotes","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:12:13.318749Z","id":"c720c86f315f8e185c08df80dc44d6423ff3e8e2008833cddfcc97a537d01422","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_export.rs:1049-1068 always calls graphs_post / graphs_post_streamed (POST create a new graph); cmd_export.rs:997 keys the record by remote_path_url(.., graph_id, &p.server_id), so the key changes every share. engine.rs:118-132 record_remote only `.insert(url, record)` into a BTreeMap<String, RemoteRecord> (engine.rs:51), replacing only an identical URL. RemoteRecord (engine.rs:63-73) has steps, last_step, head, source_stamp and no timestamp. Concern is the right kind (no current reader).","kind":"comment","references":"d041fa029e0b2e645ce28a14e08a70ac6658f9d5c9e64adaeb4bfbdde30fce82","summary":"confirmed: each share keys a new graph uuid and RemoteRecord carries no time, so entries accumulate unordered","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:12:13.318758Z","id":"e3dce0d25cf783880a24db90b6d715edd08671238391e186d5a2b94ed7b8e57e","body":{"detail":"engine.rs:41-46 SyncRecord has `modified: Option<DateTime<Utc>>`, `size: Option<u64>`; is_unchanged (engine.rs:~221-232) requires `modified.is_some() || size.is_some()` before matching. engine.rs:69-72 RemoteRecord.source_stamp is a String from stamp_string (engine.rs:94-103), `to_rfc3339_opts(AutoSi, true)` + `/` + size, which yields \"/\" for (None, None). A reader must re-render and special-case \"/\". Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"9739e6ca149231bef8e1191c55a20b8a7af594b34ce790f71129088e1a999414","summary":"confirmed: source_stamp is a rendered string while SyncRecord keeps typed modified/size, and \"/\" encodes unknowable","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:12:32.405346Z","id":"9df13b2b1e9598a3e8ba12aacced6f931a0381e2b8dc8e61fcc9b7a182e5e49d","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:28-52: `SyncRecord` carries `remotes` with `#[serde(default)]` and no `deny_unknown_fields`; `git show origin/ben/jsonl-streaming-upload:crates/path-cli/Cargo.toml` is version 0.29.0 and its engine.rs has no `deny_unknown_fields` either, while its `flush_writes` replaces records with `.extend(records)` (line 171) and `record_artifact` with `.insert(artifact.id.clone(), record)` (line 214), both through `update_manifest` (load, mutate, save whole file). So an older binary drops unknown `remotes` on load and writes the file back without them. engine.rs:556 still says `parse {}; delete it to re-sync from scratch`. CHANGELOG.md:19-20 says only `Manifests without the field load unchanged`. No non-test code reads `.remotes` (grep shows only engine.rs:129/245 carry-forward and test assertions), so nothing fails before merge: concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"752df0eb3fd7e4dff7330d7360191353d222cbfa90e1b4f81db389badfec04bc","summary":"confirmed: remotes live in manifest.json, which a 0.29.0 binary rewrites wholesale without them, and the parse error still says to delete the file","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:15:25.633767Z","id":"885b7f732e8e929ed36a82db44c7d11a5e64b333ba172d3f1dbaacd2cb4a85e9","body":{"detail":"Owner decision, 2026-10-13. The binaries that drop the unknown remotes field and write the manifest back are already shipped, and two path binaries routinely coexist on one machine (cargo bin and the curl installer's ~/.local/bin; the plugins pick whichever is first on PATH), so a version marker or serde flatten in the manifest only protects forward. The records move to their own file, $CONFIG_DIR/remotes.json: { version: 1, sessions: { <the artifact key the manifest uses for the session>: { <path API URL per f626e758>: RemoteRecord } } }. Written atomically (temp file + rename) under the existing manifest lock, after the upload succeeds, where record_remote writes today. On first load any remotes found inside manifest.json are lifted into the new file once and no longer written to the manifest. RemoteRecord and the engine code that builds it are unchanged. This also settles 752df0eb: the manifest stays a rebuildable cache index whose parse-error advice to delete it remains safe, and the remotes file is the one non-rebuildable state under ~/.toolpath.","kind":"decision","references":"125f455d83db973bdcc6d850aecebc301196e8f41a7d581404c944acc87f8f77","suggested_fix":"Add sync::remotes (load/save of remotes.json with version field, atomic write, same lock); route record_remote to it; one-time lift of SyncRecord.remotes from the manifest on load, then stop serializing that field; tests: a 0.29-shaped manifest round-trip leaves remotes.json intact, and the lift migrates and clears. Not implemented yet; lands in the #356 fix pass.","summary":"Decided: remote records move out of manifest.json into their own versioned remotes.json","tags":["review:pr-356-qual-2","decision","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T16:15:25.681257Z","id":"9b635c20bf933eb8fc830b0d66aefe7d32aef70719ff1ab11f4f10aa76cd54ae","body":{"detail":"See the decision on 125f455d (2026-10-13): remotes.json is the durable, non-rebuildable file; manifest.json remains a cache index that the parse-error message may safely advise deleting.","kind":"decision","references":"752df0eb3fd7e4dff7330d7360191353d222cbfa90e1b4f81db389badfec04bc","summary":"Settled by the 125f455d decision: records leave manifest.json for their own file, so deleting the manifest no longer loses them","tags":["review:pr-356-qual-2","decision","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
